---
// Timeoff — Stripe Redesign case study. Same stripped system as /jpl-redesign: painterly
// /work backdrop kept as-is, NO mat — a plain left-hung column straight on the painting.
// Red is a whisper (kicker/title), quiet warm-ink body, bare wide media. One beat per screen.
// Keeps the signature before/after slider, de-framed to match the bare-media look. Inter.
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Stripe Redesign — Timeoff</title>
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400..800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
    <script is:inline>
      // Paint the mobile theme from the first frame: stamp <html> before <body> renders,
      // so there's no flash of the desktop (red text / textured bg) on navigation.
      if (window.matchMedia && window.matchMedia('(max-width: 768px)').matches) {
        document.documentElement.classList.add('is-mobile');
      }
    </script>
    <script is:inline>
      if (sessionStorage.getItem('navTL')) {
        document.documentElement.classList.add('pre-tl');
        sessionStorage.removeItem('navTL');
      }
    </script>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main class="page">
      <!-- ——— hero ——— -->
      <section class="panel hero-panel">
        <header class="hero">
          <p class="kicker reveal">Web Design · Front End · Animation · 2026</p>
          <h1 class="title reveal">Stripe Redesign</h1>
          <p class="subtitle reveal">Landing Page Redesign – Unofficial</p>
          <p class="scroll-hint reveal">Scroll ↓</p>
        </header>
      </section>

      <!-- ——— before/after slider ——— -->
      <section class="panel">
        <div class="media reveal">
          <p class="caption">Drag to compare — the original, and my redesign..</p>
          <div class="ba-slider" id="ba-slider" style="--pos: 50%;">
            <img class="ba-img ba-after" src="/stripe-mine.png" alt="My Stripe landing page redesign" draggable="false" width="1999" height="1070" />
            <img class="ba-img ba-before" src="/stripe-original.png" alt="Stripe's current landing page" draggable="false" width="1998" height="1060" />
            <div class="ba-divider"></div>
            <button class="ba-handle" type="button" aria-label="Drag to compare the original and the redesign">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M9 6l-4 6 4 6M15 6l4 6-4 6"/></svg>
            </button>
            <span class="ba-label ba-label-left">Original</span>
            <span class="ba-label ba-label-right">Redesign</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ——— intro ——— -->
      <section class="panel text-panel">
        <div class="text reveal">
          <p class="lead">I&rsquo;ve fallen in love with web design, and crafting/tailoring a web experience that users will resonate with and enjoy. I take a lot of pride in capturing the essence of the company, person, whatever I&rsquo;m designing the website for.</p>
          <p>After building Bird Dog and UI Playground, and realizing how much I loved product/web design, I really wanted a challenge. I wanted to take something that was widely considered &ldquo;perfect&rdquo; or &ldquo;the gold standard&rdquo; and see if I could do better&hellip; and I think I did.</p>
          <p>I knew that in the tech/startup space, Stripe was considered THE BEST website/landing page. I had seen plenty of videos online of design walkthroughs of Stripe&rsquo;s website, and witnessed all of the tech nerds drooling over it. So I went to their site to take a closer look, and wouldn&rsquo;t you know&hellip; they just launched a fresh redesign&hellip; perfect timing. And now my challenge just became even harder, but onwards I went.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ——— demo 1: the current site ——— -->
      <section class="panel">
        <figure class="media reveal">
          <p class="caption">Stripe&rsquo;s current landing page..</p>
          <div class="vimeo-wrapper">
            <iframe loading="lazy" src="https://player.vimeo.com/video/1195796116?autopause=0&muted=1&controls=0&loop=1&title=0&byline=0&portrait=0" frameborder="0" allow="autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen></iframe>
          </div>
        </figure>
      </section>

      <section class="panel text-panel">
        <div class="text reveal">
          <p>So above is Stripe&rsquo;s fresh new landing page&hellip; what is widely considered to be the gold standard for a SaaS landing page. If you&rsquo;re not in the know, startup founders&rsquo; kryptonite is making a landing page that converts &mdash; it&rsquo;s like a big deal, for real.</p>
          <p>My initial reaction to the site was genuinely that it was way too overwhelming, and that I had no idea what Stripe actually was/did after scrolling through. Obviously I know what Stripe is, but when I try to look through the lens of someone with little to no prior knowledge of the company, I was shocked at how little the site actually serviced them. It is an endless pit of attention-grabbing animations (impressive animations tho) and information dumps.</p>
          <p>The main issue in this regard is that Stripe has become something HUGE. They have so many products and offerings (good for them) that it&rsquo;s almost impossible to make a landing page that can communicate all of it effectively, and identify what YOU as the user are even looking for. It&rsquo;s a mess.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="panel text-panel">
        <div class="text reveal">
          <p>The other main issue, and this one is particularly interesting, is that Stripe becoming the gold standard for a SaaS landing page has started to actually become an issue for them. Other SaaS companies have taken notes from the Stripe playbook (blurple, logo carousels, animations) &mdash; so much so that every SaaS nowadays has a landing page that looks like an offspring of Stripe&rsquo;s. My thinking was &ldquo;Stripe&rsquo;s landing page looks no different than a small, new SaaS startup&rsquo;s landing page.&rdquo;</p>
          <p>The last issue I have energy to write about right now is similar &mdash; a company as big and successful as Stripe SHOULD NOT HAVE A WEBSITE THAT LOOKS LIKE ANY OTHER STARTUP. I mean seriously, Stripe&rsquo;s whole landing page is full of things that say &ldquo;look at me!&rdquo; &ldquo;Look at what I can do!&rdquo; &ldquo;Spend money on me!&rdquo; Cmon&hellip; we&rsquo;re past that now.</p>
          <p>And don&rsquo;t even get me started on that horrible footer.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ——— demo 2: the redesign scroll-through ——— -->
      <section class="panel">
        <figure class="media reveal">
          <p class="caption">A scroll-through of my redesign..</p>
          <div class="vimeo-wrapper">
            <iframe loading="lazy" src="https://player.vimeo.com/video/1195796991?autopause=0&muted=1&controls=0&loop=1&title=0&byline=0&portrait=0" frameborder="0" allow="autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen></iframe>
          </div>
        </figure>
      </section>

      <section class="panel text-panel">
        <div class="text reveal">
          <p>Okay, now that all of that is off my chest, we can get into my redesign. There are a few &ldquo;pillars&rdquo; I wanted to work around:</p>
          <ol class="list">
            <li>Make the landing page simpler, but still capture Stripe&rsquo;s playfulness.</li>
            <li>Emphasize the human element. Stripe has what no fresh SaaS has &mdash; MILLIONS of users who use their products every day in so many cool and different ways. Let&rsquo;s highlight that.</li>
            <li>Trim the fat. We don&rsquo;t want a bottomless pit of info and animations. Reduce it to what is necessary to communicate what Stripe is, how Stripe can help you, and convert the user.</li>
            <li>Whisper, don&rsquo;t shout. A company like Stripe does not need to flaunt logos every chance it gets, or show off every single product feature it can think of. These things almost have the opposite effect when you reach a certain level of growth&hellip; ya know?</li>
          </ol>
          <p>I think the final product came out really good. Take the time to open the actual site and scroll through it &mdash; there&rsquo;s some fun little easter eggs.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ——— demo 3: hero ——— -->
      <section class="panel">
        <figure class="media reveal">
          <p class="caption">The hero section..</p>
          <div class="vimeo-wrapper">
            <iframe loading="lazy" src="https://player.vimeo.com/video/1195797423?autopause=0&muted=1&controls=0&loop=1&title=0&byline=0&portrait=0" frameborder="0" allow="autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen></iframe>
          </div>
        </figure>
      </section>

      <section class="panel text-panel">
        <div class="text reveal">
          <p>The hero section was naturally the first idea I had worked out in my head before even starting. Stripe&rsquo;s actual hero is notoriously cool, especially with the wave animation. But I really wanted to communicate something more&hellip; human? As I mentioned, one of Stripe&rsquo;s most powerful assets is that they have millions of REAL users who use their products every day. Highlighting &ldquo;Stripe moments&rdquo; felt like a good way to connect to a potential user &mdash; maybe they could see themselves reflected in one of the clips.</p>
          <p>I love the animation of the &ldquo;Get started&rdquo; button &mdash; I really took a liking to Stripe&rsquo;s parallelogram logo and wanted to incorporate it in some fun ways.</p>
          <p>I put the &ldquo;Trusted By&rdquo; section tucked away on the bottom right, because this is where &ldquo;whisper, don&rsquo;t shout&rdquo; comes into play. It&rsquo;s there, people will see it and be impressed, but it doesn&rsquo;t need to do the work for us.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ——— demo 4: why stripe ——— -->
      <section class="panel">
        <figure class="media reveal">
          <p class="caption">The &ldquo;Why Stripe?&rdquo; section..</p>
          <div class="vimeo-wrapper">
            <iframe loading="lazy" src="https://player.vimeo.com/video/1195798006?autopause=0&muted=1&controls=0&loop=1&title=0&byline=0&portrait=0" frameborder="0" allow="autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen></iframe>
          </div>
        </figure>
      </section>

      <section class="panel text-panel">
        <div class="text reveal">
          <p>The &ldquo;Why Stripe?&rdquo; section took me the longest, even though it looks the simplest visually. I had originally built out a section very similar to Stripe&rsquo;s bento-style section under their hero, with a bunch of animated cards. That sucked. And that is where this airy, light design framework was really born &mdash; I started with a more true rendition of Stripe&rsquo;s design, then ended up going the complete opposite direction, and I&rsquo;m happy I did.</p>
          <p>The job of this section is to literally answer &ldquo;why Stripe?&rdquo; It can be applied to whatever you&rsquo;re building: a SaaS, an on-demand product, e-commerce. It works at 10 customers, and it works at 10 million. And we know you&rsquo;re worried about the things that might go wrong&hellip; but we already thought of those and handle them ourselves.</p>
          <p>This was all meant to almost read the user&rsquo;s mind &mdash; &ldquo;will this work for X?&rdquo; &ldquo;what happens if Y?&rdquo; &ldquo;can it handle Z?&rdquo; I tried to answer all of those questions before the user can even finish their thought.</p>
          <p>I love the airy design of this section. The mix of images, editorial-style text, and animations (that were incredibly hard to build lol) all tie together really well. I also really enjoy the scroll-triggered color fill of the globe, and how the GDP stat line sort of slots right in at the bottom.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ——— demo 5: integration ——— -->
      <section class="panel">
        <figure class="media reveal">
          <p class="caption">The integration section..</p>
          <div class="vimeo-wrapper">
            <iframe loading="lazy" src="https://player.vimeo.com/video/1195798294?autopause=0&muted=1&controls=0&loop=1&title=0&byline=0&portrait=0" frameborder="0" allow="autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen></iframe>
          </div>
        </figure>
      </section>

      <section class="panel text-panel">
        <div class="text reveal">
          <p>The integration section was a surprising win. I really struggled to think of a concept &mdash; all I knew was that I wanted to communicate that with one simple integration, you had access to a whole suite of products.</p>
          <p>After mulling ideas over for a day or two, I decided to just go to the source. Even though I had criticisms of Stripe&rsquo;s site, there were some really well-done elements. One section I loved was &ldquo;The backbone of global commerce&rdquo; &mdash; I always scrolled back to that one. So I essentially rebuilt it in my version and turned it into a nice editorial-style section.</p>
          <p>The particle animations surprisingly weren&rsquo;t too hard to build, and they&rsquo;re pretty close to the quality of Stripe&rsquo;s. I picked one backdrop I really liked and ran with it &mdash; this &ldquo;sunrise&rdquo; color palette.</p>
          <p>The funny part is that when building this section I accidentally made the canvas too small. The whole thing was supposed to be full-bleed across the page, but it came out as this rectangle framed onto the page, and I thought it was beautiful. A happy mistake. Last was to add in the text elements, the cherry on top &mdash; a mix of inspiration from Apple, OpenAI, and modern print editorials.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ——— demo 6: final CTA + footer ——— -->
      <section class="panel">
        <figure class="media reveal">
          <p class="caption">The final CTA section and footer..</p>
          <div class="vimeo-wrapper">
            <iframe loading="lazy" src="https://player.vimeo.com/video/1195798596?autopause=0&muted=1&controls=0&loop=1&title=0&byline=0&portrait=0" frameborder="0" allow="autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen></iframe>
          </div>
        </figure>
      </section>

      <section class="panel text-panel">
        <div class="text reveal">
          <p>Okay, finally we&rsquo;re at the end. This section wraps it all up and acts as the final CTA for the user. We had our initial CTA in the hero, but maybe they weren&rsquo;t convinced and wanted to scroll&hellip; this is where we try to convert if they feel we earned their trust.</p>
          <p>I had an idea for a &ldquo;sandwich&rdquo; layout that I feel like I don&rsquo;t see often. Most sites have a hero, sections to scroll through, and then a lousy closing section. What if we added a really nice closing hero? I love it, and I don&rsquo;t know why it isn&rsquo;t more common.</p>
          <p>On Stripe&rsquo;s site I also really enjoyed the images they made for some of the notable companies using Stripe &mdash; realistic images with the parallelogram shape snuck in. This one was made for Hertz, but I used it as the hero image and framed the CTA inside the logo.</p>
          <p>You&rsquo;ll also notice the brazen logo carousel. I did feel we should include a more obvious, trust-building carousel somewhere &mdash; I tucked a small one in the main hero, and a larger one felt right at the bottom. And the footer&hellip; I didn&rsquo;t do much work on it, but it&rsquo;s at least better than that encyclopedia Stripe has on theirs.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ——— closing: visit the live site ——— -->
      <section class="panel closing-panel">
        <div class="closing reveal">
          <p class="caption">See it for yourself..</p>
          <div class="visit-block">
            <img class="visit-note" src="/click_to_visit_trim.png" alt="Click to visit the site" width="340" height="64" />
            <a class="omnibox" href="https://stripe-redesign.vercel.app/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open the live Stripe redesign at stripe-redesign.vercel.app">
              <svg class="omnibox-lock" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="currentColor"><path d="M11 7V5a3 3 0 0 0-6 0v2H4v7h8V7h-1zm-4-2a1 1 0 0 1 2 0v2H7V5z"/></svg>
              <span class="omnibox-url">stripe-redesign.vercel.app</span>
              <svg class="omnibox-arrow" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg>
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ——— next project ——— -->
      <section class="panel next-panel">
        <a class="next reveal" href="/ui-playground">
          <span class="next-kicker">Next</span>
          <span class="next-title">UI Playground</span>
        </a>
      </section>
    </main>

    <nav class="chrome" aria-label="site">
      <a class="label tl work grow" href="/work">Work</a>
      <a class="label tr info grow" href="/information">Information</a>
    </nav>

    <style>
      :root {
        --fg: #d6352a;                       /* red — accent (kicker, title) */
        --ink: #26241f;                      /* warm near-black — body reading ink */
        --muted: rgba(38, 36, 31, 0.5);      /* captions */
      }
      * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
      html { background: #eef0ec; scroll-behavior: smooth; }
      body {
        /* painterly backdrop, kept as-is — content sits straight on the painting, no mat */
        background: #eef0ec url('/work-bg.png') center / cover no-repeat fixed;
        color: var(--ink);
        font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
        -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
        min-height: 100vh;
      }

      /* ——— the column: one plain centered measure; painting shows in the gutters ——— */
      .page {
        position: relative;
        z-index: 1;
        max-width: min(92vw, 1080px);
        margin: 0 auto;
        animation: page-in 0.55s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1) backwards;
        transition: opacity 0.3s ease-out;
      }
      @keyframes page-in {
        from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(10px); }
        to   { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
      }
      .page.leaving { opacity: 0; }
      @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
        .page { animation: none; }
        .page.leaving { opacity: 1; transition: none; }
      }

      /* ——— one beat per screen, everything hung to the same left edge ——— */
      .panel {
        min-height: 100vh;
        display: grid;
        align-content: center;
        justify-items: start;
        padding: 12vh 0;
      }

      /* ——— hero ——— */
      .hero { text-align: left; }
      .kicker { font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--fg); margin-bottom: 1.4rem; }
      .title { font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 7vw, 5.4rem); font-weight: 400; line-height: 1; letter-spacing: -0.012em; color: var(--fg); }
      .subtitle { font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 7vw, 5.4rem); font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.04; letter-spacing: -0.012em; color: var(--fg); margin-top: 0.2rem; }
      .scroll-hint { font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 3.5rem; }

      /* ——— bare media — no frame, no shadow, demos/screengrabs all at 1060px ——— */
      .media { max-width: 1060px; width: 100%; }
      .caption { font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--muted); letter-spacing: 0.01em; margin-bottom: 0.7rem; }
      .media :global(img), .media .vimeo-wrapper { display: block; }
      .vimeo-wrapper { position: relative; width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 1920 / 1036; overflow: hidden; background: #ddd; }
      .vimeo-wrapper iframe { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border: none; }

      /* ——— before/after slider (bare, to match the demos) ——— */
      .ba-slider {
        position: relative;
        width: 100%;
        aspect-ratio: 1998 / 1060;
        overflow: hidden;
        cursor: ew-resize;
        user-select: none;
        -webkit-user-select: none;
        touch-action: none;
        background: #ddd;
      }
      .ba-img { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; object-position: top left; }
      .ba-before { clip-path: inset(0 calc(100% - var(--pos)) 0 0); z-index: 2; }   /* original on top, clipped left of the divider */
      .ba-after { z-index: 1; }
      .ba-divider { position: absolute; top: 0; bottom: 0; left: var(--pos); width: 2px; margin-left: -1px; background: #fff; box-shadow: 0 0 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.25); z-index: 3; pointer-events: none; }
      .ba-handle { position: absolute; top: 50%; left: var(--pos); transform: translate(-50%, -50%); width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 50%; background: #fff; border: none; box-shadow: 0 2px 12px rgba(0,0,0,0.28); display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; color: #5f6368; cursor: ew-resize; z-index: 4; }
      .ba-handle svg { width: 22px; height: 22px; }
      .ba-label { position: absolute; bottom: 14px; font-size: 0.6rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #fff; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.5); padding: 5px 11px; border-radius: 999px; z-index: 5; pointer-events: none; }
      .ba-label-left { left: 14px; }
      .ba-label-right { right: 14px; }

      /* ——— text: quiet, left-hung, one calm treatment (ref: Studio Small) ——— */
      .text-panel p {
        max-width: 58ch;
        font-size: clamp(1.02rem, 1.35vw, 1.16rem);
        font-weight: 400;
        line-height: 1.7;
        color: var(--ink);
      }
      .text { max-width: 58ch; }
      .text p { max-width: none; }
      .text p + p { margin-top: 1.4rem; }
      .text .lead { color: #1a1916; }
      .text .list { max-width: none; margin: 1.3rem 0; padding-left: 1.4rem; }
      .text .list li { font-size: clamp(1.02rem, 1.35vw, 1.16rem); line-height: 1.7; color: var(--ink); }
      .text .list li + li { margin-top: 0.7rem; }

      /* ——— reveal-on-scroll: rises into frame, weighted easing ——— */
      .reveal {
        opacity: 0;
        transform: translateY(40px);
        transition: opacity 1s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1), transform 1s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
        will-change: opacity, transform;
      }
      .reveal.in { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
      @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
        .reveal { opacity: 1 !important; transform: none !important; transition: none; }
      }

      /* ——— closing: visit the live site ——— */
      .closing { width: 100%; max-width: 1060px; }
      .visit-block { max-width: 340px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 1rem; }
      .visit-note { display: block; width: 300px; max-width: 100%; height: auto; opacity: 0.8; margin: 0 0 0.9rem 0.5rem; pointer-events: none; }
      .omnibox { position: relative; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; padding: 12px 18px; background: #f1f3f4; border: 1px solid #e4e6e8; border-radius: 999px; text-decoration: none; overflow: hidden; transition: background 0.25s ease, box-shadow 0.3s ease, transform 0.25s ease; }
      .omnibox:hover { background: #eceef0; box-shadow: 0 8px 30px rgba(0,0,0,0.08); transform: translateY(-1px); }
      .omnibox-lock { width: 13px; height: 13px; color: #5f6368; flex-shrink: 0; }
      .omnibox-url { flex: 1; font-family: 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 0.85rem; color: #202124; white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; }
      .omnibox-arrow { width: 16px; height: 16px; color: #5f6368; flex-shrink: 0; transition: transform 0.25s ease, color 0.25s ease; }
      .omnibox:hover .omnibox-arrow { transform: translateX(4px); color: #202124; }
      .omnibox::after { content: ''; position: absolute; top: 0; left: -60%; width: 55%; height: 100%; background: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, rgba(255,255,255,0.75), transparent); transform: skewX(-20deg); pointer-events: none; }
      .omnibox:hover::after { animation: omnibox-shimmer 0.9s ease; }
      @keyframes omnibox-shimmer { from { left: -60%; } to { left: 130%; } }

      /* ——— next project ——— */
      .next-panel { min-height: 70vh; }
      .next { display: inline-flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.4rem; text-decoration: none; }
      .next-kicker { font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.18em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); }
      .next-title { font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.4rem); font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: -0.012em; color: var(--fg); transition: transform 0.5s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1); }
      .next:hover .next-title { transform: translateX(0.6rem); }

      /* ——— corner chrome (matches /work) ——— */
      .chrome { position: fixed; inset: 0; z-index: 4; pointer-events: none; mix-blend-mode: difference; }
      .label { position: fixed; font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.18em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #fff; }
      .grow { pointer-events: auto; text-decoration: none; white-space: nowrap; line-height: 1; will-change: font-size; transition: font-size 0.62s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1), letter-spacing 0.62s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1), font-weight 0.62s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1); }
      .grow:hover { font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
      .work:hover { font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 6vw, 5.6rem); }
      .info:hover { font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 3.9rem); }
      html.pre-tl .grow { transition: none; }
      html.pre-tl .work { font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 6vw, 5.6rem); font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
      .tl { top: 1.9rem; left: 2.2rem; }
      .tr { top: 1.9rem; right: 2.2rem; }
      /* First-paint mobile theme (html.is-mobile set by the head script): kill the desktop
         red text + textured background on the very first frame, before the @media rules
         resolve — this is what removes the flash on navigation. */
      html.is-mobile { --fg: #141414; }
      html.is-mobile, html.is-mobile body { background: #fff; }

      /* ——— Mobile: white/black StudioSmall retheme + natural stacked scroll
         (shared project-page format; see jpl-redesign) ——— */
      @media (max-width: 768px) {
        :root { --fg: #141414; --ink: #1a1a1a; --muted: rgba(20, 20, 20, 0.46); }
        html { background: #fff; }
        body { background: #fff; overflow-x: hidden; }
        .page { max-width: 100%; margin: 0; padding: 0 1rem; }
        .panel { min-height: auto; padding: 4.5vh 0; }
        .hero-panel { min-height: 74vh; padding-top: 20vh; }
        .next-panel { min-height: auto; padding: 6vh 0 12vh; }
        .title, .subtitle { font-size: clamp(2rem, 8.5vw, 2.5rem); }
        .kicker { color: var(--muted); }
        .scroll-hint { margin-top: 2.4rem; }
        .media { max-width: 100%; }
        /* before/after slider: bigger touch handle */
        .ba-handle { width: 52px; height: 52px; }
      }
      /* Touch devices have no hover, so the nav enlarge — both the :hover growth and
         the persisted cross-page handoff (pre-tl/pre-tr) — only reads as a broken
         giant word. Keep the nav labels small and static on mobile. */
      @media (hover: none) {
        .grow, .grow:hover, html.pre-tl .grow, html.pre-tr .grow {
          font-size: 0.72rem !important;
          font-weight: 600 !important;
          letter-spacing: 0.16em !important;
        }
      }

    </style>

    <script>
      window.addEventListener('pointermove', () => {
        document.documentElement.classList.remove('pre-tl');
      }, { once: true });

      // ——— smooth exit: gentle opacity dip, then navigate (internal links only) ———
      const page = document.querySelector('.page');
      const reduceMotion = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
      document.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
        const a = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest('a');
        if (!a) return;
        const href = a.getAttribute('href');
        if (!href || a.target === '_blank' || a.hasAttribute('download')) return;
        if (e.metaKey || e.ctrlKey || e.shiftKey || e.altKey || (e as MouseEvent).button !== 0) return;
        const url = new URL(href, location.href);
        if (url.origin !== location.origin || url.pathname === location.pathname) return;
        e.preventDefault();
        if (a.classList.contains('work')) sessionStorage.setItem('navTL', '1');
        if (a.classList.contains('info')) sessionStorage.setItem('navTR', '1');
        if (reduceMotion) { window.location.href = url.href; return; }
        page?.classList.add('leaving');
        setTimeout(() => { window.location.href = url.href; }, 200);
      });
      window.addEventListener('pageshow', (e) => { if (e.persisted) page?.classList.remove('leaving'); });

      // ——— reveal-on-scroll ———
      const reveals = document.querySelectorAll('.reveal');
      if (reduceMotion) {
        reveals.forEach((el) => el.classList.add('in'));
      } else {
        const io = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
          entries.forEach((en) => {
            if (en.isIntersecting) { en.target.classList.add('in'); io.unobserve(en.target); }
          });
        }, { threshold: 0.2, rootMargin: '0px 0px -12% 0px' });
        reveals.forEach((el) => io.observe(el));
      }

      // ——— Vimeo demos: muted, play only while in view, booted lazily ———
      function initVimeoDemos() {
        const iframes = document.querySelectorAll('.vimeo-wrapper iframe');
        if (!iframes.length) return;
        const attach = () => {
          const players = new WeakMap();
          // create each player only when its demo first scrolls into view, so we never
          // boot all of them at once (six simultaneous handshakes tripped "Player error")
          const observer = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
            entries.forEach((entry) => {
              const iframe = entry.target as HTMLIFrameElement;
              if (entry.isIntersecting) {
                let player = players.get(iframe);
                if (!player) {
                  player = new (window as any).Vimeo.Player(iframe);
                  player.setVolume(0);
                  players.set(iframe, player);
                }
                player.ready().then(() => player.setVolume(0)).then(() => player.play()).catch(() => {});
              } else {
                const player = players.get(iframe);
                if (player) player.pause().then(() => player.setCurrentTime(0)).catch(() => {});
              }
            });
          }, { threshold: 0.5 });
          iframes.forEach((iframe) => observer.observe(iframe));
        };
        if ((window as any).Vimeo && (window as any).Vimeo.Player) {
          attach();
        } else {
          let api = document.getElementById('vimeo-api') as HTMLScriptElement | null;
          if (!api) {
            api = document.createElement('script');
            api.id = 'vimeo-api';
            api.src = 'https://player.vimeo.com/api/player.js';
            document.head.appendChild(api);
          }
          api.addEventListener('load', attach, { once: true });
        }
      }
      requestAnimationFrame(() => initVimeoDemos());

      // ——— before/after slider: drag the divider to wipe between original and redesign ———
      function initBASlider() {
        const slider = document.getElementById('ba-slider');
        if (!slider || slider.dataset.baInit) return;
        slider.dataset.baInit = '1';

        let dragging = false;
        let lastInteraction = 0;
        let tweenRAF: number | null = null;
        let idleTimer: any = null;
        const IDLE_INTERVAL = 6000;

        const setPosRaw = (pct: number) => slider.style.setProperty('--pos', pct + '%');
        const getPos = () => parseFloat(getComputedStyle(slider).getPropertyValue('--pos')) || 50;
        const setPosFromX = (clientX: number) => {
          const rect = slider.getBoundingClientRect();
          const pct = ((clientX - rect.left) / rect.width) * 100;
          setPosRaw(Math.max(0, Math.min(100, pct)));
        };
        const stopTween = () => { if (tweenRAF) { cancelAnimationFrame(tweenRAF); tweenRAF = null; } };
        const tweenTo = (target: number, duration: number, done?: () => void) => {
          stopTween();
          const start = getPos();
          const startT = performance.now();
          const ease = (t: number) => (t < 0.5 ? 2 * t * t : 1 - Math.pow(-2 * t + 2, 2) / 2);
          const step = (now: number) => {
            const t = Math.min(1, (now - startT) / duration);
            setPosRaw(start + (target - start) * ease(t));
            if (t < 1) tweenRAF = requestAnimationFrame(step);
            else { tweenRAF = null; if (done) done(); }
          };
          tweenRAF = requestAnimationFrame(step);
        };
        const nudge = () => {
          if (dragging || reduceMotion) return;
          tweenTo(33, 750, () => { setTimeout(() => { if (!dragging) tweenTo(50, 750); }, 400); });
        };
        const scheduleIdle = () => {
          clearTimeout(idleTimer);
          idleTimer = setTimeout(() => {
            if (!dragging && Date.now() - lastInteraction > IDLE_INTERVAL - 200) nudge();
            scheduleIdle();
          }, IDLE_INTERVAL);
        };
        const onInteract = () => { lastInteraction = Date.now(); stopTween(); };

        slider.addEventListener('pointerdown', (e) => {
          dragging = true; onInteract();
          try { slider.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId); } catch (_) {}
          setPosFromX(e.clientX);
        });
        slider.addEventListener('pointermove', (e) => { if (dragging) { setPosFromX(e.clientX); lastInteraction = Date.now(); } });
        slider.addEventListener('pointerup', () => { dragging = false; lastInteraction = Date.now(); });
        slider.addEventListener('pointercancel', () => { dragging = false; lastInteraction = Date.now(); });

        if (!reduceMotion) { setTimeout(nudge, 700); scheduleIdle(); }
      }
      initBASlider();
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
